# LOCAL web pointed at the DEV server's API (https://dev.book-nest.net).
# Usage: pnpm dev:web:dev (from the repo root) — no local API/Docker needed.
# Committed on purpose: contains no secrets, only public URLs.
# Field docs live in .env.local.example.
#
# Only API_BASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL change. The browser still calls
# same-origin /api on localhost:3000; Next rewrites proxy it server-side to
# API_BASE_URL, and SSR fetches hit it directly. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL stays
# localhost because the web itself runs locally.
#
# The realtime socket cannot go through that rewrite: the Next proxy does not
# perform a WebSocket upgrade, so the browser connects straight to the dev API.
# The dev server's CORS_ORIGINS already allows http://localhost:3000.
#
# Auth works through the proxy: the refresh cookie is host-only (no Domain
# attribute), so the browser scopes it to localhost:3000, and Secure cookies
# are allowed on localhost. Verified end-to-end (login → cookie → refresh).

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
API_BASE_URL=https://dev.book-nest.net
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL=https://dev.book-nest.net
